    {
      "id": "p0117-b002",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Ore is another common masculine pronoun in Japanese. It projects a sense of manliness, strength, confidence, being in charge, and/or vulgarity. As such, it's considered a bit crude, and isn't fit for formal situations or when trying to be polite. Among close friends and family, ore can instead indicate familiarity. Examples of fictional characters who use ore include:",
        "raw": "Ore is another common masculine pronoun in Japanese. It projects a sense\nof manliness, strength, confidence, being in charge, and/or vulgarity.\nAs such, it's considered a bit crude, and isn't fit for formal situations or\nwhen trying to be polite. Among close friends and family, ore can instead\nindicate familiarity. Examples of fictional characters who use ore include:",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
